<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #1130.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="514166218" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/issues/1130" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/zookeeper/pull/1130/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/pull/1130">#1130</a> from lvfangmin/ZOOKEEPER-3598

Just a small change. Check leader in `recvset` when consider notifications from the same election, and not from `outofelection`.

Parameter `n.state` is needed when creating the new `Vote` because otherwise the vote will be in a `LOOKING` state and hence `checkLeader` will fail when checking whether the leader is [`LEADING`](<a href="https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/blob/master/zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/FastLeaderElection.java#L793">https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/blob/master/zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/FastLeaderElection.java#L793</a>).

