Since authFailed is similar to session expired and is considered a fatal event, we should clean up after ourselves once we get a AuthFailed, other wise this results in an unavoidable and un-cleanable thread leak  of EventThread since the close operation is also a no-op (we return after checking for isAlive).

Author: Abhishek Singh Chouhan &lt;abhishekchouhan121@gmail.com&gt;

Reviewers: Andor Molnar &lt;andor@apache.org&gt;

<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #541.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="331282539" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/issues/541" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/zookeeper/pull/541/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/pull/541">#541</a> from abhishek-chouhan/master and squashes the following commits:

<a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/commit/c54a83a486e4b6372e7004d44d2dbd0ba7ab61bb/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/commit/c54a83a486e4b6372e7004d44d2dbd0ba7ab61bb"><tt>c54a83a</tt></a> [Abhishek Singh Chouhan] ZOOKEEPER-3059 EventThread leak in case of Sasl AuthFailed. Adding testcase for the scenario
<a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/commit/c1d9d7afe1de246ad32d43032df7bb428fcceae6/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/zookeeper/commit/c1d9d7afe1de246ad32d43032df7bb428fcceae6"><tt>c1d9d7a</tt></a> [Abhishek Singh Chouhan] ZOOKEEPER-3059 EventThread leak in case of Sasl AuthFailed

Currently, if the client is closed (rather than being remotely disconnected) there is no notification to the watcher. This means that asynchronous clients can end up waiting indefinitely for events that will never come. Watchers need to be aware that the client is closed for good.

Signed-off-by: Tim Ward &lt;timothyjwardapache.org&gt;

Note that this is a variation on a patch I produced some time ago, which was broadly accepted as a good idea, and didn't cause any problems for Curator, but was deemed by some to be too risky because it reused an existing KeeperState. This patch is therefore updated to use a new `Closed` KeeperState. Fixing this would allow me to avoid maintaining a separate fork of Zookeeper just to support this one feature!

